iquístico.", "MDTEXT.COM, INC.:MDText.com, Inc. is a publisher based in South Dartmouth, MA, known for providing medical information and guidelines.", "28-YEAR-OLD PATIENT:A 28-year-old female patient presenting with slowly progressive hirsutism and irregular menstrual cycles, suspected to have PCOS.", "NATIONAL CENTER FOR BIOTECHNOLOGY INFORMATION:The National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) is a branch of the National Institutes of Health that provides access to biomedical and genomic information.", "POLYCYSTIC OVARY SYNDROME:Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) is a prevalent endocrine disorder that primarily affects women. It is characterized by irregular menstrual cycles, elevated levels of androgens, and the presence of polycystic ovaries, which are enlarged ovaries containing small cysts on their outer edges. This hormonal disorder can lead to a range of metabolic and clinical consequences, impacting women's overall health and well-being.", "SOUTH DARTMOUTH:", "HOMA INDEX:The HOMA index is a method used to estimate insulin resistance and beta-cell function, often elevated in patients with Polycystic Ovary Syndrome.", "SLEEP APNEA SYNDROME:SLEEP APNEA SYNDROME, specifically obstructive sleep apnea syndrome, is a condition characterized by repeated interruptions in breathing during sleep. This disorder can be exacerbated by obesity, which may worsen the severity of the condition. Additionally, sleep apnea syndrome has implications for patients undergoing testosterone treatment, highlighting the need for careful management in individuals affected by this disorder.", "ERYTHROCYTOSIS:Erythrocytosis is a condition where there is an increase in red blood cells, which can be a potential adverse effect of testosterone treatment.", "ENDOMETRIAL ATROPHY:Endometrial atrophy is the thinning of the endometrial lining, which can occur as a result of testosterone treatment in transsexual men.", "HEMBREE WC:Hembree WC is an author of the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline focused on the endocrine treatment of gender-dysphoric persons. This guideline serves as a comprehensive resource for healthcare professionals regarding the appropriate endocrine interventions for individuals experiencing gender dysphoria."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}